---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ImageZoom from '../../components/ImageZoom.astro';
import StoreLink from '../../components/StoreLink.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/manual/Callout.astro';
import Keys from '../../components/manual/Keys.astro';
import { API_KEYS, LINKS } from '../../lib/links';
import { crisp } from '../../lib/screenshots';
import agent from '../../assets/manual/agent-chat.png';
import profiles from '../../assets/manual/popup-profiles.png';
import agentDark from '../../assets/manual/agent-chat-dark.png';
import profilesDark from '../../assets/manual/popup-profiles-dark.png';
import editor from '../../assets/manual/editor-panel.png';
import editorDark from '../../assets/manual/editor-panel-dark.png';
import sync from '../../assets/manual/sync.png';
import syncDark from '../../assets/manual/sync-dark.png';
import position from '../../assets/manual/position-menu.png';
import positionDark from '../../assets/manual/position-menu-dark.png';
import history from '../../assets/manual/history.png';
import historyDark from '../../assets/manual/history-dark.png';
---

<Base title="What's new in 4.0">
  <main class="prose">
    <h1>What's new in 4.0</h1>
    <Callout>
      <strong>
        Stylebot updated itself, and your styles and settings came with it.
      </strong>{' '}
      One thing moved: in Chrome and Edge the editor now opens in the side
      panel. To change that, use <strong>Position</strong> in the editor's
      <strong>⋯</strong> menu.
    </Callout>
    <p class="lede">
      Restyle any site by describing it, or by clicking. Now with dark mode,
      profiles and a side panel.
    </p>
    <nav class="release-toc" aria-label="Sections">
      <a href="#editor">Redesigned editor</a>
      <a href="#agent">Stylebot agent</a>
      <a href="#profiles">Profiles</a>
      <a href="#panel">Side panel</a>
      <a href="#history">Version history</a>
      <a href="#sync">Sync</a>
      <a href="#more">And more</a>
      <a href="#try">Try it</a>
    </nav>

    <h2 id="editor">A redesigned editor</h2>
    <figure>
      <Image
        class="shot-image is-light"
        src={editor}
        height={560}
        densities={[1, 2]}
        {...crisp(editor)}
        alt="The redesigned Basic tab, styling Hacker News with a Dracula profile"
      />
      <Image
        class="shot-image is-dark"
        src={editorDark}
        height={560}
        densities={[1, 2]}
        {...crisp(editorDark)}
        alt="The redesigned Basic tab, styling Hacker News with a Dracula profile"
      />
    </figure>
    <p>Rebuilt from the ground up, now with dark mode.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Grouped controls that show the page's own values</li>
      <li>Color palettes and an eyedropper</li>
      <li>400 Google Fonts</li>
      <li>Edit any other CSS property in place under More properties</li>
      <li>Undo and redo</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="agent">The Stylebot agent</h2>
    <figure>
      <Image
        class="shot-image is-light"
        src={agent}
        height={400}
        densities={[1, 2]}
        {...crisp(agent)}
        alt="The Chat tab after asking the agent for a calmer, Everforest-themed Google"
      />
      <Image
        class="shot-image is-dark"
        src={agentDark}
        height={400}
        densities={[1, 2]}
        {...crisp(agentDark)}
        alt="The Chat tab after asking the agent for a calmer, Everforest-themed Google"
      />
    </figure>
    <p>Describe what you want in the Chat tab and the agent writes the CSS.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Point at an element or attach a screenshot</li>
      <li>Undo any change</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      It needs your own API key. Get a <a href={API_KEYS.claude}>Claude</a>,{' '}
      <a href={API_KEYS.openai}>OpenAI</a> or{' '}
      <a href={API_KEYS.gemini}>Gemini</a> key and paste it into the Chat tab.
      Your key stays in your browser, and messages go straight to the provider.{' '}
      <a href={`${LINKS.manual}#api-key`}>See how to connect a key</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="profiles">Profiles</h2>
    <figure>
      <Image
        class="shot-image is-light"
        src={profiles}
        height={profiles.height / 2}
        densities={[1, 2]}
        {...crisp(profiles)}
        alt="The popup on a site with two profiles, Dracula and Gruvbox"
      />
      <Image
        class="shot-image is-dark"
        src={profilesDark}
        height={profilesDark.height / 2}
        densities={[1, 2]}
        {...crisp(profilesDark)}
        alt="The popup on a site with two profiles, Dracula and Gruvbox"
      />
    </figure>
    <p>
      Keep several looks for a site, like a dark one for night and a light one
      for the day, and switch between them from the editor or the popup.
    </p>

    <h2 id="panel">The side panel, or its own window</h2>
    <figure>
      <Image
        class="shot-image is-light"
        src={position}
        height={position.height / 2}
        densities={[1, 2]}
        {...crisp(position)}
        alt="The editor's menu, with Position set to the side panel"
      />
      <Image
        class="shot-image is-dark"
        src={positionDark}
        height={positionDark.height / 2}
        densities={[1, 2]}
        {...crisp(positionDark)}
        alt="The editor's menu, with Position set to the side panel"
      />
    </figure>
    <p>
      In Chrome and Edge the editor opens in the side panel. Or pop it out into
      its own window, from <strong>Position</strong> in the editor's
      <strong>⋯</strong> menu.
    </p>

    <h2 id="history">Version history</h2>
    <figure>
      <Image
        class="shot-image is-light"
        src={history}
        width={history.width / 2}
        densities={[1, 2]}
        {...crisp(history)}
        alt="Version history in Options, newest change first"
      />
      <Image
        class="shot-image is-dark"
        src={historyDark}
        width={historyDark.width / 2}
        densities={[1, 2]}
        {...crisp(historyDark)}
        alt="Version history in Options, newest change first"
      />
    </figure>
    <p>Every change is kept, and you can restore any earlier version.</p>

    <h2 id="sync">Sync</h2>
    <figure>
      <Image
        class="shot-image is-light"
        src={sync}
        width={sync.width / 2}
        densities={[1, 2]}
        {...crisp(sync)}
        alt="Options, connected to Google Drive and synced"
      />
      <Image
        class="shot-image is-dark"
        src={syncDark}
        width={syncDark.width / 2}
        densities={[1, 2]}
        {...crisp(syncDark)}
        alt="Options, connected to Google Drive and synced"
      />
    </figure>
    <p>
      Google Drive sync is more robust, and merges changes from different
      computers instead of overwriting them.
    </p>

    <h2 id="more">And more</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A new Stylebot icon</li>
      <li>
        Change Stylebot's shortcuts in your browser's shortcut settings. If you
        had changed them in Chrome or Edge, set them again there.
      </li>
      <li>Stylebot is now available in Vietnamese</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="try">Try it</h2>
    <p>
      Open any site and press <Keys keys={['alt', 'shift', 'M']} />, then go to{' '}
      <strong>Chat</strong> and describe the change you want.
    </p>
    <p>
      If Stylebot is useful to you, please rate it. It helps others find it, as
      does sharing it with a friend.
    </p>
    <p class="release-rate">
      <StoreLink index={0} format="rate" class="btn btn-primary" />
    </p>

    <p class="release-end">
      Plus lots of bug fixes. See the <a href={LINKS.changelog}>changelog</a>{' '}
      for everything in 4.0.
    </p>
  </main>
  <ImageZoom />
</Base>

<style>
  .release-toc {
    margin: 20px 0 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .release-toc a {
    padding: 7px 12px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--surface);
    font: 500 13.5px/1 var(--ui);
    color: var(--ink2);
  }

  .release-toc a:hover {
    background: var(--hover);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  h2[id] {
    scroll-margin-top: 80px;
  }

  .prose :global(.callout) {
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: var(--fill);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    font: 400 14.5px/1.55 var(--ui);
    color: var(--ink2);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .prose :global(.callout-icon) {
    flex: none;
    width: 18px;
    height: 18px;
    margin-top: 1px;
    border-radius: 9px;
    background: var(--muted);
    color: var(--surface);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font: 700 11px/1 system-ui;
  }

  .prose :global(.keys) {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 4px;
  }

  .prose :global(kbd) {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 2px 7px;
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: var(--fill);
    border: 1px solid var(--strong);
    border-bottom-width: 2px;
    font: 500 12px/1.4 var(--mono);
    color: var(--ink2);
  }

  .prose :global(.keys-sep) {
    font: 400 12px/1 var(--ui);
    color: var(--faint);
  }

  .release-rate {
    margin-top: 20px;
  }

  .release-end {
    margin-top: 56px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
</style>
